  "generated_text": "1. **Identify the points of intersection**:\n   - The lines $l$ and $m$ intersect the y-axis at $(0,6)$.\n   - Line $l$ intersects the x-axis at $(6,0)$.\n   - Line $m$ intersects the x-axis at $(3/2,0)$.\n\n2. **Calculate the area of the triangle formed by lines $l$ and $m$**:\n   - The base of the triangle is the distance between $(6,0)$ and $(3/2,0)$, which is $9/2$.\n   - The height of the triangle is $6$.\n   - The area of the triangle is $\\frac{1}{2} \\times (9/2) \\times 6 = 27$.\n\n3. **Calculate the probability**:\n   - The probability is the ratio of the area of the triangle to the area of the first quadrant, which is $27$.\n   - The probability is $\\frac{27}{27} = 1$.\n\n4. **Express the probability as a decimal**:\n   - The probability expressed as a decimal to the nearest hundredth is $\\boxed{1.00}$",
